Q.19 Consider the following context-free grammar 𝐺, where 𝑆, 𝐴, and 𝐵 are the variables 
(non-terminals), 𝑎 and 𝑏 are the terminal symbols, 𝑆 is the start variable , and the 
rules of 𝐺 are described as: 
𝑆 → 𝑎𝑎𝐵 | 𝐴𝑏𝑏 
𝐴 → 𝑎 | 𝑎𝐴         
𝐵 → 𝑏 | 𝑏𝐵         
Which ONE of the languages 𝐿(𝐺) is accepted by 𝐺?  

(A) 𝐿(𝐺)  =  {𝑎2𝑏𝑛 | 𝑛 ≥ 1} ∪ {𝑎𝑛𝑏2 | 𝑛 ≥ 1}  
(B) 𝐿(𝐺)  =  {𝑎𝑛𝑏2𝑛 | 𝑛 ≥ 1} ∪ {𝑎2𝑛𝑏𝑛 | 𝑛 ≥ 1}  
(C) 𝐿(𝐺)  =  {𝑎𝑛𝑏𝑛 | 𝑛 ≥ 1}  
(D) 𝐿(𝐺)  =  {𝑎2𝑛𝑏2𝑛 | 𝑛 ≥ 1}

